  },
  "checks": [
    {
      "topic": "six binders and original literals",
      "result": "PASS",
      "details": "Structural and six analytic binders match Header97 byte-for-byte as decoded text; all13 c/Phi/S/Rec/Hist/Delta/Prefix/m/zAt/K/Path/Psi/Gamma let declarations text-identical. No provider assumption added. R is explicit momentum negation; rate is actual sqrt eta positive-part gradient defect. Clamp agrees with94 up to bound-variable names."
    },
    {
      "topic": "target energy versus harmonic energy",
      "result": "PASS",
      "details": "U=V(x)+norm(x-y)^2/(2 eta)+norm(p)^2/2 is source3.1 target negative log density up to a constant, not the conserved centered H(y,r). From dx=sqrt eta p and dp=-(x-y)/sqrt eta-sqrt eta grad V(r), dU=sqrt eta inner(p,grad V(x)-grad V(r)). SourceA4 is derivative log nu=-dU; Header energy sign is therefore positive Iplus-Iminus."
    },
    {
      "topic": "positive-part identity and exponential sign",
      "result": "PASS",
      "details": "rate(Rz)=sqrt eta max(0,-a), so rate(z)-rate(Rz)=sqrt eta a for every real a. U(A)-U(z)=Iplus-Iminus gives -U(z)-Iplus=-U(A)-Iminus, hence the stated exp-product equality. Neither U>=0 nor rate>0 nor finite normalizer is needed."
    },
    {
      "topic": "piecewise path and intervals",
      "result": "PASS_FEASIBLE",
      "details": "The actual path is post-bounce and may be discontinuous at finite event times. Equality to each continuous arc is only required on Ioo. Lebesgue interval integrals ignore finite endpoints; congr_uIoo and integral_congr_Ioo_of_le support integrability/equality. m is retained exactly although this pointwise target does not integrate over m. The clamp affects no time in [0,T]. Reversal of the entire right-continuous path is not needed for98."
    },
    {
      "topic": "producer limitations",
      "result": "PASS_WITH_EXPLICIT_NEW_OBLIGATIONS",
      "details": "Public94 supplies forward rate integrability/sum only. Its private arc_integral/finite_arc_integral/actual_arc cannot be imported by their source names. R-rate whole-path integrability and energy telescoping are genuinely new finite adapters; use public93 live-arc law or a separately justified shared extraction. Public97 provides terminal identity but its full product-volume result is not a premise of98."
    },
    {
      "topic": "zero cases",
      "result": "PASS",
      "details": "n0 has one arc and empty tuple. T0,n0 gives A=z and zero integrals. T0,n>0 admits no strict tuple. Rank0 has U=V(0), which may be nonzero or negative, but constant phase and zero rates/increment. Zero reflection normal gives S=id and rate0 at that phase, without a nonzero-normal or positive-event premise. Norm-square derivative works at zero vectors."
    },
    {
      "topic": "pinned APIs and feasibility",
      "result": "PASS_FEASIBLE_NOT_PROVED",
      "details": "Confirmed HasFDerivAt.comp_hasDerivAt, HasDerivAt.norm_sq, inner_gradient_left/right, intervalIntegral.integral_eq_sub_of_hasDerivAt, integral_comp_sub_right, integral_congr_Ioo_of_le and the existing94 finite adjacent-arc proof. ContDiff2 implies the needed V differentiability/gradient continuity. Eta>0 supplies sqrt positivity and (sqrt eta)^2=eta. No further analytic assumption identified."
    }
  ],
